{#- Atlas — the way into the records (decisions 1, 2, 3, 10, 15).

  Every record the build put on the site, listed. Without this page the roadmap, the design
  authorities and the standalone documents all live at URLs nothing links to, and a site whose
  records cannot be reached fails Atlas's own premise invisibly — the pages exist, so nothing looks
  broken.

  **Two kinds, and the difference is stated rather than hidden.** A Markdown record is rendered by
  Atlas, so its page is a rendering and the file remains the authority (decision 2). A standalone
  document is copied byte-for-byte and never templated (decision 10) — it is not an Atlas page at
  all, it is the file itself, styles and scripts and all. A reader who follows one link lands on
  something Atlas made; a reader who follows the other lands on the document its author made. That
  is worth a word, not a shrug.

  Generated from the very lists the pages and the copies come from (decision 3), so it cannot name
  something the build did not write, or omit something it did. Grouped by the directory each file
  lives in, because the repository's own shape is the only grouping Atlas is entitled to invent.

  Data this layout expects:
    groups — [{ dir, entries: [{ title, path, url, kind }] }], in path order, where `kind` is
             "rendered" or "copied"
    project, repo, title — see base.njk
-#}
{% extends "base.njk" %}

{% block bodyClass %}page page-records{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Project depth</a></p>
<h1>Records</h1>
<p class="lede">Every record on this site, in the shape of the repository that holds it. Atlas is never the record: where a page and its file disagree, the file is right.</p>

{% for group in groups %}
<section class="record-group">
<h2><code>{{ group.dir }}</code></h2>
<ul class="named-refs">
{% for entry in group.entries %}
<li data-kind="{{ entry.kind }}"><a href="{{ entry.url }}">{{ entry.title }}</a> <span class="where">{{ entry.path }}{% if entry.kind == "copied" %} — a standalone document, served exactly as it is in the repository{% endif %}</span></li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
